Note on scope, because a licence disclaimer is a poor place to be vague:

This software provides a development-time control. It reduces the chance that an
unsupported completion declaration is made and makes such declarations visible
when they are made. It does not guarantee correctness, and its enforcement can be
bypassed deliberately (see `spec/enforcement-boundary.md` for exactly where the
boundary falls). A passing gate means "sufficiently supported by the recorded
evidence", never "absolutely proven". Do not treat it as a security boundary or
as a substitute for engineering judgement.
